# Portfolio Backend (FastAPI + MongoDB)

Backend for a proof-of-work portfolio site: services list, reviews, a contact
form, editable social links, and an admin panel to manage all of it.

## Setup

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
cp .env.example .env
# then edit .env with your real MongoDB URI, a random JWT_SECRET,
# and the admin username/password you want on first run
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

Visit `http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs` for interactive API docs (Swagger UI) —
useful for testing every endpoint before you wire up the frontend.

## How admin login works

- On first startup, if no admin exists yet in the database, one is created
  from `ADMIN_USERNAME` / `ADMIN_PASSWORD` in your `.env`.
- `POST /admin/login` with that username/password returns a JWT `access_token`.
- Send that token on every admin request as a header:
  `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
- `POST /admin/change-password` lets you change it afterwards — do this once
  you've confirmed login works, so the `.env` password isn't the real one.

## Endpoints

### Public (no auth)
| Method | Path | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/services` | List all services offered |
| GET | `/reviews` | List all reviews |
| POST | `/reviews` | Submit a review `{name, message, rating}` |
| POST | `/messages` | Submit a contact message `{name, contact, message}` |
| GET | `/social` | List social links (use this to populate the Instagram modal) |
| POST | `/admin/login` | Log in, get a token |

### Admin (needs `Authorization: Bearer <token>`)
| Method | Path | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/admin/services` | Add a service |
| PUT | `/admin/services/{id}` | Edit a service |
| DELETE | `/admin/services/{id}` | Delete a service |
| DELETE | `/admin/reviews/{id}` | Delete a review |
| GET | `/admin/messages` | View contact form submissions |
| DELETE | `/admin/messages/{id}` | Delete a message |
| POST | `/admin/social` | Add a social link `{platform, url}` |
| PUT | `/admin/social/{id}` | Edit a social link's URL |
| DELETE | `/admin/social/{id}` | Delete a social link |
| POST | `/admin/change-password` | Change the admin password |

## Deploying (Render/Railway/PythonAnywhere)

- Set the same env vars from `.env.example` in your host's dashboard.
- Start command: `uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT`
- Use MongoDB Atlas's free tier for `MONGO_URI` if you don't have Mongo hosted
  elsewhere already.
- Once deployed, put your real frontend URL(s) in `CORS_ORIGINS` — the `*`
  default is fine for local testing but you'll want to lock it down for prod.

## Frontend notes

- The "Order now" button doesn't need its own endpoint — just `GET /social`,
  find the `instagram` entry, and open your contact modal with that URL.
- Review form and contact form are both public — no login needed for visitors.